cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Freehand, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Freehand: learning a silently changed tool from the consequences of one's own strokes"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark and research code base: an agent closes hand-drawn squares on a simulated page through a pen plotter
  and a camera; partway through, the tool silently changes. Freehand scores whether the agent transfers a model of
  the change to new targets (the first-try learning curve), not only whether it completes the page.
authors:
  - family-names: Chaudhary
    given-names: Raghav
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-29"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - multimodal agents
  - adaptation
  - tool use
